113
00:04:47,557 --> 00:04:48,729
write clean functions.

114
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,537
That all starts with the parameters.

115
00:04:52,115 --> 00:04:54,666
Limit the number of function parameters and

116
00:04:54,763 --> 00:04:56,271
try to keep the list short.

117
00:04:56,849 --> 00:04:59,721
Consider using dictionaries or objects to

118
00:04:59,818 --> 00:05:02,530
group multiple parameters into one parameter

119
00:05:02,947 --> 00:05:04,664
and therefore make sure that functions are

120
00:05:04,953 --> 00:05:05,482
easy to call

121
00:05:06,076 --> 00:05:08,309
and the code where a function does get

122
00:05:08,341 --> 00:05:10,686
called is easy to read and understand.

123
00:05:11,377 --> 00:05:13,288
Now, when we talk about the function body,

124
00:05:13,722 --> 00:05:16,581
clean functions should be small functions

125
00:05:16,854 --> 00:05:18,588
that do just one thing.

126
00:05:19,504 --> 00:05:21,881
Now, you learned that this one thing is

127
00:05:21,913 --> 00:05:24,531
related to the levels of abstraction. So

128
00:05:24,563 --> 00:05:26,474
therefore, always make sure that there is no

129
00:05:26,651 --> 00:05:29,301
big gap between the level of abstraction

130
00:05:29,301 --> 00:05:30,971
implied by a function name

131
00:05:31,534 --> 00:05:33,879
and the actual code which can be found in

132
00:05:33,879 --> 00:05:36,333
the function and that you're not mixing

133
00:05:36,365 --> 00:05:38,337
multiple levels of abstraction in one

134
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:38,818
function.

135
00:05:39,795 --> 00:05:41,847
Also, of course, don't repeat yourself.

136
00:05:42,521 --> 00:05:44,637
That should be obvious, but it is important.

137
00:05:45,246 --> 00:05:48,244
And avoid unexpected side effects. Side

138
00:05:48,244 --> 00:05:51,161
effects are okay, but if they're unexpected,

139
00:05:51,514 --> 00:05:54,207
then a function is not easy to understand

140
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,291
and therefore it's not written in a clean

141
00:05:56,387 --> 00:05:56,644
way.

142
00:05:57,269 --> 00:05:59,754
Now often you're also going to use control

143
00:05:59,754 --> 00:06:02,708
structures. And there, one suggestion is

144
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:05,327
that you're using positive wording if

145
00:06:05,456 --> 00:06:07,078
possible and if it makes sense.

146
00:06:07,801 --> 00:06:09,858
And of course, avoid deep nesting.

147
00:06:10,436 --> 00:06:13,441
For example, by using these guards, these if

148
00:06:13,569 --> 00:06:16,043
checks at the beginning of a function which

149
00:06:16,301 --> 00:06:19,016
cancel the function execution early if some

150
00:06:19,048 --> 00:06:20,156
condition is not met.

151
00:06:20,879 --> 00:06:24,526
Or avoid deep nesting by extracting logic

152
00:06:24,526 --> 00:06:26,487
and control structures into separate

153
00:06:26,583 --> 00:06:28,820
functions. That is always something which

154
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:29,271
