157
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,547
I showed it to you throughout this course,

158
00:06:38,175 --> 00:06:41,411
and use real errors instead of synthetic

159
00:06:41,556 --> 00:06:44,744
errors replicated with if statements. This

160
00:06:44,857 --> 00:06:47,575
also is a key part of writing clean code.

161
00:06:49,133 --> 00:06:51,126
Now, often you're also going to work with

162
00:06:51,206 --> 00:06:54,033
