168
00:07:06,527 --> 00:07:08,903
Depending on what you need, it's okay to use

169
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,343
either of these 2 kinds of objects but you

170
00:07:11,343 --> 00:07:13,768
should not mix them. Either have real

171
00:07:13,816 --> 00:07:16,433
objects with an API of methods which are

172
00:07:16,481 --> 00:07:18,825
exposed or just use data containers.

173
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:22,229
Mixing them often results in unclean code.

174
00:07:23,303 --> 00:07:25,836
Clean classes also should be small and you

175
00:07:25,852 --> 00:07:27,840
achieve that by focusing on one

176
00:07:27,936 --> 00:07:28,833
responsibility,

177
00:07:29,378 --> 00:07:31,254
which does not mean that a class should only

178
00:07:31,302 --> 00:07:34,204
